# Hot fraction sets the resting temperature
# Four equal source portions isolate one variable: how much hot water enters
# the final mixture. The thermometer should rise monotonically with that share.
register lv2
add v1 water 200mL @ 80C
new
add v2 water 200mL @ 20C
new
mix v1 0.2 v2 0.8 into v3
measure v3 thermometer
new
add v4 water 200mL @ 80C
new
add v5 water 200mL @ 20C
new
mix v4 0.4 v5 0.6 into v6
measure v6 thermometer
new
add v7 water 200mL @ 80C
new
add v8 water 200mL @ 20C
new
mix v7 0.6 v8 0.4 into v9
measure v9 thermometer
new
add v10 water 200mL @ 80C
new
add v11 water 200mL @ 20C
new
mix v10 0.8 v11 0.2 into v12
measure v12 thermometer
# These vessels are adiabatic constant-heat-capacity models. Real containers
# lose heat, and the bench does not predict pouring or cooling rates.
